meta {
  name: Read game notes
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/me/games/{{gameId}}/note
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

docs {
  Free-text notes on one game in the caller's library: where you left off, what to
  do next, the things a notes-app file would hold.

  Owner-only, and deliberately with no public mirror under /users/{username}. That
  is also what keeps notes out of the cached library payload: they are long (20,000
  characters, vs 1,000 for a wishlist note) and the public read is prerendered.

  A game with no note yet answers 200 with `{"body": "", "updatedAt": null}` rather
  than 404. "You have not written one" is a value, not an error; 404 stays reserved
  for "not your game", as everywhere under /me.

  - 200 `{ body, updatedAt }` — updatedAt is ISO-8601 UTC, or null when unwritten
  - 404 no such game in the caller's library
}
